# 3D MRI Phase Unwrapping

3D phase processing pipeline for MRI phase images in Python.

If you use this code in your work, please cite:
```
Bartz, KM, et al., "A Three-Dimensional Phase Unwrapping Method Applied to Paramagnetic Rim Lesion Visualization," in [Proceedings of ISMRM Workshop on White Matter: MR Imaging and Beyond, Marseille, France, October 14 -- 16, 2026], 2026.
```
and
```
Blake E. Dewey. (2022). Laplacian-based Phase Unwrapping in Python. Zenodo. [https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7198990](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7198991)
```

## Install with pip
```bash
pip install 3D_laplacian_phase_unwrap
```

## Basic Usage
```bash
unwrap-phase-3D /path/to/phase_image.nii.gz
```
This will produce an unwrapped phase image in the same directory as the input image with `_unwrapped_3D` appended to the filename.


### CLI Options
| Option            | Description                                                 | Default  |
|-------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------|
|                   | Path to phase image                                         | Required |
| `-o`/`--output`   | Output path                                                 | Optional |

Using the `--output` option will save the unwrapped image to that path. 
If not provided, the unwrapped image will be saved to the same directory as the input image with `_unwrapped_3D` appended to the filename (before the `.nii.gz`).
